{{name}} dev
A work loop for the reviews and pull requests that reach you.

USAGE
  {{command}} <command> [arguments]

GET STARTED
  init                   Set up from zero: config, agent homes, the app
  doctor                 Diagnose the setup without changing anything

PULL REQUESTS
  act                    Resolve a unit's open items, replies as drafts
  address                Triage the reviews and failing checks of yours
  nudge                  Ask whoever it waits on for the next step
  review                 Review someone else's pull request in its own worktree
  start                  Start new work from a brief
  take-over              Make a pull request someone else opened yours
  remove                 Delete the workspace of a merged or closed one

WHAT WAITS ON YOU
  status                 Pull requests by view, those needing you first
  tui                    The same views in the terminal, one-key actions
  open                   The cockpit, a workspace or a pull request
  outbox                 Drafts waiting for your approval, and yours
  task                   Make this agent session a run of a task
  explore                Open pull requests of others to help on

AUTOMATION
  plan                   What the workflows would do now, and why
  pause/resume           Stop or restart automatic rounds
  track/untrack          Follow a pull request out of scope, or stop
  mute/unmute            Leave or rejoin the pending views
  workflows              The facts and steps a workflow can use

PROFILE
  profile show           The blocks that apply to a repository
  profile where          The block a new rule goes in
  profile add            Add a rule to the profile
  profile check          Load the profile and list its problems
  profile try            A review round that publishes nothing
  profile schema         The JSON Schemas of the profile files, for editors

SLACK
  slack login/logout     Connect to Slack, or disconnect
  slack status           Who you are logged in to Slack as
  slack send             Post as you to a thread, channel or person
  slack follow/unfollow  Admit every message of a thread, or stop

SETUP
  install                Write the hooks, MCP and skills into agent homes
  app install            macOS: the app, menu bar and the daemon at login
  trust                  Trust a repository in an agent home
  uninstall              Take out what install and app install set up
  store migrate          Migrate the store to this release's schema
  store restore          Put a backup of the store back
  config get             Print a configuration value
  version                Print the version

TROUBLESHOOTING
  timings                Review, merge and turn durations, waits, tokens
  intake                 Follow, start or cancel an intake
  brief refresh          Make a pull request's brief again
  turn show              A pull request's turns and their records
  probe                  Prove an agent home end to end

FOR AGENTS AND SCRIPTS
  instructions           Run a turn by hand from an agent session
  turn end/answer        Record how a turn ended; read your answer
  hook                   The agent hooks install writes
  serve                  Run the daemon
  app                    macOS: the menu bar and notifications

Run '{{command}} <command> --help' for its flags and examples.
Docs: https://{{name}}hq.github.io/{{name}}/
